        "answer": {
          "short": "a and d; c and h.\n\nEach pair has equal gradients.",
          "worked": "Read each gradient from $y=mx+c$, rearranging where necessary.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}y&=7-3x&&\\text{(b)}\\\\x-1&=\\frac12y&&\\text{(d)}\\\\y&=2x-2&&\\text{(d)}\\\\2y&=x+7&&\\text{(f)}\\\\y&=\\frac12x+\\frac72&&\\text{(f)}\\\\3y&=8-x&&\\text{(g)}\\\\y&=-\\frac13x+\\frac83&&\\text{(g)}\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe gradients of a–h are respectively $2,-3,-2,2,\\frac13,\\frac12,-\\frac13,-2$. Therefore a and d are parallel, and c and h are parallel, because each pair has equal gradients.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
